      "story": "The relativity papers came from a clerk who had failed the entrance exam to Zurich Polytechnic the first time and been told he would \"never amount to anything\". He kept the job at the patent office for the freedom it gave his mind. When the Nazis came to power in 1933 he was visiting the United States and never returned; his refugee status made him a public symbol of the scientific emigration, and his letter to President Roosevelt in 1939 helped set in motion the Manhattan Project he later called the flame he should never have touched.\n",
