      "summary": "The mathematician Einstein called \"the most significant creative mathematical genius thus far produced since the higher education of women began\". Emmy Noether, at Göttingen in 1918, proved the theorem that carries her name: for every symmetry of a physical system there is a conserved quantity — the conservation of energy follows from symmetry in time, of momentum from symmetry in space. It is the deep reason entire laws of physics exist.\n\nBarred for years from an official post because she was a woman, she lectured under Hilbert's name and stayed through the Weimar years until the Nazis expelled her. She died in 1935 in the United States, two years after fleeing there.\n",
