      "story": "Nash's famous result was famously short: a single page, barely a proof by modern standards, full of ideas bigger than its prose. The equilibrium named for him generalised Cournot's duopoly into every possible game — and its radical novelty was its modesty. It says nothing about fairness or efficiency; it only says what must eventually stop moving.\n",
