      "significance": "Nearly every market you actually deal with — airlines, telecoms, banks, phone networks — is an oligopoly. Textbooks start at the ideal and walk toward reality; oligopoly is where the theory stops pretending. It is also the reason cartels exist, why prices rarely move even when costs do, and why competition watchdogs spend their lives watching a handful of firms.\n",
