      "summary": "The second year of psychology at Lagos State University, where introspection turns into experiment. Students learn to distrust their own common sense: experimental methods, the physiological bases of behaviour, social and developmental psychology, personality and its assessment, and the statistics that give the findings their spine.\n\nThis is the year the psychology student discovers that the mind is a testable system — that a well-run experiment can falsify what everyone \"knew\". It feeds directly into behavioral economics, where the same experimental methods undo the clean assumptions of economic choice.\n",
