      "gift": "b. 1995",
      "summary": "A 200-level economics student at LASU reflecting on the year the discipline stops being common sense. Emeka reads Cournot the way his lecturers intend — as the moment a market became a machine you may take apart on paper.\n\nHis voice is the archive's reminder that theory lives one desk at a time: \"The first year asked what a market is. The second year asks you to prove it.\"\n",
