      "gift": "b. 1996",
      "summary": "A 200-level psychology student at LASU on the year common sense goes on trial. Amaka's course teaches her that the mind is a thing to be measured, not guessed at — and that the experiment is the only referee that matters.\n\nHer voice ties psychology to the economic archive: the same experimental honesty that tests human behaviour feeds the behavioral economics that repairs Adam Smith's clean assumptions.\n",
