      "significance": "Software engineering matters because software is now the world's wiring. Trains, banks, planes and hospitals all run on code, and code is the first engineering material that can be changed as easily as it can be broken. The discipline exists to make that change deliberate — reviewed, tested and reversible — instead of a gamble.\n",
