      "location": "Unix culture → the pull request",
      "summary": "The practice of having another human read your code before it ships. Review catches what tests cannot — naming, design, missed edge cases, and the question every maintainer asks: will someone understand this in a year? It formalised out of Unix culture, was standardised by the pull-request workflows of GitHub, and is now the most broadly accepted quality ritual in the discipline.\n\nDone well, review is also the field's seminar: the juniors learn from the seniors by reading their code, and the seniors learn by explaining their own.",
