      "id": "nato-1968",
      "type": "event",
      "label": "The NATO Software Crisis, 1968",
      "tag": "Software Engineering",
      "dates": [
        1968
      ],
      "location": "Garmisch, Germany",
      "summary": "The conference where \"software engineering\" was named. In 1968 the NATO Science Committee gathered in Garmisch, Germany to confront the software crisis — projects overrunning, failing, and costing more than any mechanical construction could. The term software engineering was proposed as an aspiration and a promise: that building software could become a discipline with foundations, like building bridges.\n",
      "vector": {
        "software": 1,
        "craft": 0.9,
        "system": 0.8,
        "programming": 0.8,
        "industry": 0.7,
        "model": 0.6
      },
      "community": "the software craft",
