          "body": "Reports from Göttingen describe a young lecturer, Werner Heisenberg, who has set down the behaviour of the atom not as objects moving through space but as tables of numbers that merely predict what may be observed. Colleagues admit the mathematics is flawless and the meaning obscure. Learned opinion is divided on whether this is a new science or a new mysticism."
